From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Hope <djhope@btinternet.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:53:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] um: darwin: align native window end to the host page

The host reserves a 16 KiB-aligned window. A 4 KiB-aligned start+length
can end one guest page short of that reservation, so a user munmap that
the kernel splits at uml_darwin_native_end still overlaps the host
window. darwin_uml_vm_unmap_generation then returns EINVAL and
darwin_tlb_invalidate_range panics (seen with Firefox DOM Worker on the
iOS Simulator).

Align the published native end up to the 16 KiB host page so TLB flushes
split at the same bound the host classifies.
---
 arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c b/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c
index a350b79721d49850c56f2e1f4868323504cf54c7..087d82c25f1cab8281d0aac3947c87677be42f74 100644
--- a/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c
@@ -491,7 +491,31 @@ static unsigned long __init get_top_address(char **envp)
 		os_warn("Darwin native window exceeds guest address limit\n");
 		exit(1);
 	}
-	uml_darwin_native_end = native_start + memory + auxiliary;
+	/*
+	 * The host reserves whole Darwin host pages (16 KiB on Apple silicon,
+	 * including the iOS Simulator). A window whose 4 KiB-aligned length
+	 * is not a host-page multiple is rounded out at both ends, and the
+	 * kernel image is loaded at that reserved base. start + length then
+	 * falls short of the host window end by less than one host page, so
+	 * a user munmap that reaches the kernel's end still overlaps the
+	 * host window; darwin_uml_vm_unmap_generation returns EINVAL and
+	 * darwin_tlb_invalidate_range panics. Align the published end up so
+	 * TLB flushes split at the same bound the host classifies.
+	 */
+	{
+		const unsigned long host_page = 16UL * 1024;
+		unsigned long end = native_start + memory + auxiliary;
+
+		end = (end + host_page - 1) & ~(host_page - 1);
+		if (end > UML_DARWIN_GUEST_ADDRESS_LIMIT ||
+		    end < native_start + memory + auxiliary) {
+			os_warn("Darwin native window exceeds guest address limit\n");
+			exit(1);
+		}
+		uml_darwin_native_end = end;
+	}
+	os_info("Darwin native window %#lx-%#lx (host-page aligned)\n",
+		native_start, uml_darwin_native_end);
 	return uml_darwin_native_end;
 #else
 	unsigned long top_addr = (unsigned long) &top_addr;
